# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the whole 2.3GB working tree is sent to the daemon and much
# of it is baked into the image. Everything excluded here is either regenerated
# during the build, or is runtime/host state that the container must not carry.
#
# Do NOT exclude web/bower_components: gulpfile.js bundles tinymce, simplemde,
# inputmask and material-design-icons from it, and core/header.php serves
# flag-icon-css from it at runtime.

# Node dependencies - the builder stage runs `npm install` and `cd web && npm
# install` itself, so any host-installed copy is dead weight (~513MB).
**/node_modules

# Runtime data directory (~269MB, mostly app/data/upgrades - a vendored copy of
# an older release - plus logs and uploads). The Dockerfile recreates the
# directory, and in production the app_data volume mounts over it. Keep only the
# two directory-protection stubs that are tracked in git.
app/data/*
!app/data/index.php
!app/data/.htaccess

# MySQL bind-mount data for the dev/testing/prod compose stacks (~103MB). These
# are host database files; `COPY docker/ ...` would otherwise pull them into the
# builder stage.
docker/*/db_data*
docker/mysql8*

# Build and release output - regenerated by `ant build` / release.sh (~784MB).
build/
releases/

# Version control and editor state (~207MB).
.git
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.vagrant/

# Test artifacts and local QA output.
test/frontend/node_modules/
test/frontend/cypress/videos/
test/frontend/cypress/screenshots/
test/ai-agent-tests/

# Docs are not served by the application.
docs/

# Local config and secrets that must never reach an image.
app/config-dev.php
app/icehrm.key
icehrm.key
.env
*.log

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.swp
SECURITY_AUDIT.md
